K1 and the KCI door's test hooks

Apply to the edgetpu driver import in a development kernel tree (only three files
under drivers/edgetpu/ are tracked there, so the bring-up door arrives as files).

  edgetpu: janeiro: refuse a second power-up in the same boot

  After a power down the GSA/AON island stays unclocked (AON_* read 0xdeadfeed),
  GSA state stays 2 and the next power_up times out. Count the boot's power-ups
  and refuse the next request at once with -EBUSY, naming it in the log.

  edgetpu: widen the KCI send door and report its answers

  kci_payload holds 16 pages and the iremap allocation rounds up to the payload;
  kci_last returns the last code; kci_addr names a fixed descriptor address
  instead (K2 fault injection; the firmware validates it, see TPU-PLAN rev 45).

--- a/drivers/edgetpu/edgetpu-pm.c
+++ b/drivers/edgetpu/edgetpu-pm.c
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 	/* Power up counter. Protected by @lock */
 	int power_up_count;
 	/* Total power-ups in this boot; never reset. Protected by @lock */
+	int power_up_total;
 	/* Flag indicating a deferred power down is pending. Protected by @lock */
 	bool power_down_pending;
 	/* Worker to handle async power down retry */
@@ -57,9 +58,23 @@
 		if (etpm->p->power_down_pending) {
 			etpm->p->power_down_pending = false;
 		} else {
+			/*
+			 * K1: the TPU does not come back in the same boot. After a power
+			 * down the GSA/AON island stays unclocked (AON_* read 0xdeadfeed)
+			 * and the next power_up times out. Refuse it at once, and say so,
+			 * instead of stalling a client for the whole timeout.
+			 */
+			if (etpm->p->power_up_total) {
+				etpm->p->power_up_count--;
+				etdev_err(etpm->etdev,
+					  "K1: power-up %d refused; the TPU cannot come back in this boot\n",
+					  etpm->p->power_up_total + 1);
+				return -EBUSY;
+			}
 			ret = etpm->p->handlers->power_up(etpm);
 			if (!ret) {
 				edgetpu_mailbox_restore_active_mailbox_queues(etpm->etdev);
+				etpm->p->power_up_total++;
 			}
 		}
 	}
